  "body": "Only collaborators can set labels, so a contributor's claim is a comment. This makes that explicit and keeps the `claimed` label in sync with it, both ways (user, 2026-11-08: \"a comment should suffice ... if we come across a claimed issue thru comment we should just label it as such - and vice versa if they remove their comment, remove their claim label for em as part of maintenance.. Otherwise the comment stands as claimed.\").\n\n- **AGENTS.md** - \"A claim comment is a claim\" replaces \"Outside contributors' claims count\":\n  - check the issue's comments before claiming; a claim comment by anyone but the owner account means the issue is taken, label or not;\n  - mirror it: `claimed` + assignee (label alone if GitHub refuses the assignee) + one reply;\n  - withdrawn = deleted: if the claim comment is deleted or the claimant comments `unclaim`, remove the label and assignment and say the issue is free;\n  - a contributor's claim has no 4 h timer - it stands while the comment exists; agent claims keep the 4 h rule.\n- **`/review-prs` step 4** - now \"Mirror claim comments - add and withdraw\": the add query also accepts `/claim` and looks back 7 days; a new withdraw pass checks every open `claimed` issue for the claim behind it and drops labels whose contributor comment is gone. A label set by hand by a collaborator (no claim comment, no \"Claim recorded\" reply) is left alone.\n- `docs/decisions/comment-claims.md` records the choice and what was dropped (a `/claim` Action).\n\nChecked: the add query runs against the live repo and lists today's claim comments (37 across bherbruck, mkinney, seelesturm, linuxguy123, austin62jake).\n\nChangelog: none\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
